From 6a28002ae7ffbeb1ba607bac239e0f1e3b2ba325 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ben Joldersma <bennidhamma@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 02:27:04 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] [COSMIC] Follow COSMIC's glass opacity setting

COSMIC lets users choose how see-through its frosted windows are
(Settings > Desktop > Appearance). In its theme config, "frost
thickness" picks an entry of the "alpha_map", the alpha of window
backgrounds, and "glass opacity" shifts the whole map.

CosmicGlassSettings reads and watches these config entries (and the
light/dark mode) on a blocking sequence when the desktop is COSMIC.
GlassFrameService::AdjustTintOpacityForDesktop() maps the glass frame's
tint so that COSMIC's default alpha gives the default tint, stretching
the ranges on either side to fit, so the browser follows both sliders
live.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
